{{nihongo|'''Kirishima-Jingū'''|霧島神宮|}}, also called Takachiho-no-mine-jina (the highest peak of [[Mount Kirishima]]) is a Shinto shrine located in [[Kirishima, Kagoshima|Kirishima]], [[Kagoshima prefecture]], [[Japan]]. 

It is dedicated to [[Konohanasakuya-hime]], [[Hoori]], [[Toyotama-hime]], [[Ugayafukiaezu]], [[Tamayori-bime]] and Ninigi-no-mikoto (?). This shrine holds several [[Important Cultural Properties of Japan|Important Cultural Properties]], such as ''Honden''・''Heiden''・''Haiden'' （本殿・幣殿・拝殿）, ''Tōrōka'' （登廊下）, ''Chōkushiden'' （勅使殿） etc. It has been destroyed several times by [[volcanic]] [[eruption]]s.[http://onehundredmountains.blogspot.com/2010/01/nihon-hyakumeizan-in-search-of-ground_15.html]

